  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "A sophomore Computer Science student is frustrated with boring college lectures. Professor X agreed to give him some questions; if the student answers all questions correctly, then minimum attendance criteria will not apply to him.\n\nProfessor X chooses a sequence A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ and asks QQQ queries. In each query, the student is given an integer PPP; he has to construct a sequence B1,B2,…,BNB_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_NB1​,B2​,…,BN​, where P⊕Ai=BiP \\oplus A_i = B_iP⊕Ai​=Bi​ for each valid iii (⊕\\oplus⊕ denotes bitwise XOR), and then he has to find the number of elements of this sequence which have an even number of 111-s in the binary representation and the number of elements with an odd number of 111-s in the binary representation. Help him answer the queries.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N,Q≤1051 \\le N, Q \\le 10^51≤N,Q≤105",
      "T⋅(N+Q)≤4⋅106T \\cdot (N+Q) \\leq 4 \\cdot 10^6T⋅(N+Q)≤4⋅106",
      "1≤Ai≤1081 \\le A_i \\le 10^81≤Ai​≤108 for each valid iii",
      "1≤P≤1051 \\le P \\le 10^51≤P≤105",
      "**The input/output is quite large, please use fast reading and writing methods.**",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (30 points):** N,Q≤1,000N, Q \\le 1,000N,Q≤1,000"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and QQQ.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\nQQQ lines follow. Each of these lines contains a single integer PPP describing a query.",
    "outputFormat": "For each query, print a single line containing two space-separated integers ― the number of elements with an even number of 111-s and the number of elements with an odd number of 111-s in the binary representation.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1\n6 1\n4 2 15 9 8 8\n3",
        "output": "2 4",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nExample case 1: The elements of the sequence BBB are P⊕4=7P \\oplus 4 = 7P⊕4=7, P⊕2=1P \\oplus 2 = 1P⊕2=1, P⊕15=12P \\oplus 15 = 12P⊕15=12, P⊕9=10P \\oplus 9 = 10P⊕9=10, P⊕8=11P \\oplus 8 = 11P⊕8=11 and P⊕8=11P \\oplus 8 = 11P⊕8=11. The elements which have an even number of 111-s in the binary representation are 121212 and 101010, while the elements with an odd number of 111-s are 777, 111, 111111 and 111111."
      }
    ]
  },
